From 0dc7d708252ecff3cb7e314e436b1742c7fb02d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:34:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): re-check create_overlap inside the insert's
 write transaction [daveey]

On 11-03 a worker's kanban_create (t_01a19f0a4cc8b092) and ci-main-watch's
`hermes kanban create` (t_01a19f0a4d82213d) were inserted 186 ms apart and both
own test_termux_assembly_permissions. The overlap check reads the board outside
create_task's transaction (and the CLI runs placement/ask checks in between), so
each process passed it before the other's row existed (#732 "Known limit").

kanban_overlap.check() now returns an AfterCreate whose .guard is passed to
kb.create_task(insert_guard=...) by the tool, CLI and REST entries. The guard runs
inside the INSERT's BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction and re-runs the same match
(_find, same exemptions and gateway set) against open cards of the target board
created since the first check began; a hit raises OverlapRefused, which rolls
the create back, and the entry returns the same create_overlap payload (event
recorded as before). The first full check (all boards, replica) is unchanged;
races across boards/gateways stay a documented limit.

Tests: tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_race.py replays the real 11-03 pair
in two processes (tool + CLI, both orders) held at a barrier after the first
check: main lands 2 cards, this lands 1 and refuses the other. Cost: median of
50 non-matching tool creates 16.6-19.0 ms before vs 17.5-19.6 ms after.

To keep code-health caps: _create_session_id split out of _handle_create, and
_project_branch_name moved to kanban_db_creation.project_branch_name.
